Z||000000||maryjane||08-18-2001||01:51 AM||||I usually stay up pretty late, go to bed around 2:am even on work nights(a hamburger a week and an hour's sleep is all anybody needs) I notice the # of posts pick up after midnight. How many of you stay up REAL late and read this forum? Do your bosses ever ask why you look so tired in the mornings? I know by 5pm the next day, I'm draggin my rear end, but I do it again the next night too.<P>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 08-18-2001).]<BR>I'm editing to pose a small question about the tech section. The reason I'm posting here is because this is where all the interest seems to be. Why are there so many replies here in OT and so few in Tech? 40 threads in each section. Very few single digit replies in OT but almost all in Tech are single, with a lot that go unanswered (zero replies). Seems like the same few people do most of the answering in tech, I'm not gonna name anybody. It's pretty disheartening when your Fiero is down and no one answers a question. (I know, hardly anyone uses the 'search' utility and you old hands have answered most of em a thousand times) Maybe there is a lot of emailing going on to help out and we don't see it, or maybe no one knows a solution, but I think some of us have just lost interest. I'm one that has a lot of interest, but not much knowledge. Compare the two sections and see if you don't think we should try a little harder. It's pretty hard to get excited about football or NASCAR when your ride is sitting OOC in the drive. Sorry about the rant. I'm through now.<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||5
